\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The Son of God goes forth to war,
\par A kingly crown to gain;
\par His blood-red banner streams afar:
\par Who follows in His train?
\par Who best can drink His cup of woe,
\par Triumphant over pain,
\par Who patient bears his cross below,
\par He follows in His train.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The martyr first, whose eagle eye
\par Could pierce beyond the grave,
\par Who saw his Master in the sky,
\par And called on Him to save;
\par Like Him, with pardon on His tongue
\par In midst of mortal pain,
\par He prayed for them that did the wrong:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. A glorious band, the chosen few
\par On whom the Spirit came,
\par Twelve valiant saints, their hope they knew,
\par And mocked the cross and flame;
\par They met the tyrant's brandished steel,
\par The lion's gory mane,
\par They bowed their necks the death to feel:
\par Who follows in their train?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. A noble army, men and boys,
\par The matron and the maid,
\par Around the Saviour's throne rejoice,
\par In robes of light arrayed;
\par They climbed the steep ascent of heaven,
\par Through peril, toil, and pain:
\par O God, to us may grace be given
\par To follow in their train.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

